    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A south Indian kingdom ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#wadiyar-dynasty">Wodeyar dynasty</a>, which grew from a Vijayanagara <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#vassal">vassal</a> into a regional power.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a> it built a modern army with French-trained infantry and iron-cased rockets.</li><li>It fought four wars with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#east-india-company">East India Company</a> and fell when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#srirangapatna">Srirangapatna</a> was stormed in 1799.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#tipus-tiger">Tipu's Tiger</a>, a wooden automaton of a tiger attacking a European soldier that contains a small organ, was taken from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#srirangapatna">Srirangapatna</a> and is now in the V&amp;A in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#london">London</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

